Upstream-Status: Pending
Exit: Drop when gnome-build-meta's initramfs carries these modules itself.
Subject: initramfs: add USB root, LUKS AES-NI, Intel I2C input and virtiofs

uas lets roots on UAS USB adapters mount; usb-storage declines UAS-capable
devices and leaves them for uas. aesni_intel lets dm-crypt pick the
accelerated AES-XTS at unlock instead of the generic fallback, which stays
in use for the life of the mapping. Intel LPSS, the DesignWare I2C PCI glue
and Intel pinctrl back i2c-hid keyboards at the passphrase prompt. fs/fuse
brings virtiofs so the image boots in bcvk ephemeral VMs.

